Below are the attractions that are currently topping the “Our top picks” (trending) list for Oxford.  All of them have **free cancellation** (so you can change plans if needed) and are highly rated by travelers.  Prices are shown in USD (the system reports them that way) – you’ll see the local GBP price at checkout.

| # | Attraction | What Makes It Great for a Family | Price (per adult) | Rating & Reviews* | Quick Tips |
|---|------------|--------------------------------|-------------------|-------------------|------------|
| **1** | **University of Oxford Student‑led Walking Tour** | A lively, 2‑hour walk led by current Oxford students.  You’ll hear stories about the colleges, the Bodleian Library, and hidden corners that kids love. | **US $38.98** | 4.8 ★ (101 reviews – 96 % “highly recommended”) | • Book the **family‑friendly slot** (usually mornings).<br>• Wear comfortable shoes – the route is mostly flat but includes cobblestones.<br>• Free cancellation. |
| **2** | **City Sightseeing Oxford Hop‑on Hop‑off Bus Tour** | Open‑top double‑deck bus that stops at all the major sights (Christ Church, Radcliffe Camera, Botanic Garden, etc.).  Kids can hop on/off as they wish, making it perfect for a flexible day. | **US $24.70** | 4.5 ★ (21 reviews – 100 % “highly recommended”) | • Grab a **family ticket** (2 adults + 2 children) for a small discount.<br>• Use the audio guide (available in several languages). |
